data: {"item":{"encrypted_content":"The UI seems fine: label, input aria-label, alert role. Test expects rows with data-testid=\"project-row\". They are there. However tests fail to find project row after creation. Possibly due to missing page reload after creation? The test uses createProject helper to fill input and click button, then expects projectRow(page, name.trim()) visible. Might be because after creation, the list is not updated? In renderRoot, after createProject, they call await renderList(); That fetches loadProjects which fetches from API. API POST returns 201 with JSON. The DB insertion should work. Maybe SQLite sync API is not persisted? Use sqlite.DatabaseSync which works but maybe not in Node 22? But likely works.\n\nThe test failure indicates after creating project with trimmed name, project row not visible. Could be that the API response for GET returns rows ordered by id, but they inserted but maybe missing commit? Using DatabaseSync, exec automatically commits.\n\nCheck that POST returns JSON with name and id; createProject on client uses fetch and if not ok, throw error; else returns json but not used. Works.\n\nPotential issue: the client uses fetch with relative '/api/projects' which is fine.\n\nMaybe the server's static fallback for SPA causing path issues after navigation? Not relevant.\n\nMaybe the test environment expects the page to have a button labeled \"Create project\" (exact) and input with role textbox name \"Project name\". The HTML includes \u003clabel\u003e and \u003cinput id=\"project-name\" aria-label=\"Project name\"\u003e. That's good.\n\nBut test maybe using getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Project name', exact: true }) which uses accessible name; with aria-label, accessible name is \"Project name\". Good.\n\nThe failure may be due to trimming? In test they sometimes prepend spaces to test whitespace handling; they call fill with either name.trim() ? projectName(name) : '  ' + projectName(name) + '  '. They then call createProject(page, name.trim()). In our code, we trim input.value.trim() before sending, so whitespace should be trimmed. Good.\n\nMaybe the server's POST body parsing: getJsonBody reads data as string and JSON.parse; but request with Content-Type application/json works.\n\nPotential bug: The server's GET /api/projects returns rows ordered by id (SELECT id, name FROM projects ORDER BY id). That's fine.\n\nWhy rows not found? Perhaps the static files not being served for SPA after POST? Not.\n\nLet's try to manually test via curl.","id":"rs_839355","summary":[{"text":"The UI seems fine: label, input aria-label, alert role. Test expects rows with data-testid=\"project-row\". They are there. However tests fail to find project row after creation. Possibly due to missing page reload after creation? The test uses createProject helper to fill input and click button, then expects projectRow(page, name.trim()) visible. Might be because after creation, the list is not updated? In renderRoot, after createProject, they call await renderList(); That fetches loadProjects which fetches from API. API POST returns 201 with JSON. The DB insertion should work. Maybe SQLite sync API is not persisted? Use sqlite.DatabaseSync which works but maybe not in Node 22? But likely works.\n\nThe test failure indicates after creating project with trimmed name, project row not visible. Could be that the API response for GET returns rows ordered by id, but they inserted but maybe missing commit? Using DatabaseSync, exec automatically commits.\n\nCheck that POST returns JSON with name and id; createProject on client uses fetch and if not ok, throw error; else returns json but not used. Works.\n\nPotential issue: the client uses fetch with relative '/api/projects' which is fine.\n\nMaybe the server's static fallback for SPA causing path issues after navigation? Not relevant.\n\nMaybe the test environment expects the page to have a button labeled \"Create project\" (exact) and input with role textbox name \"Project name\". The HTML includes \u003clabel\u003e and \u003cinput id=\"project-name\" aria-label=\"Project name\"\u003e. That's good.\n\nBut test maybe using getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Project name', exact: true }) which uses accessible name; with aria-label, accessible name is \"Project name\". Good.\n\nThe failure may be due to trimming? In test they sometimes prepend spaces to test whitespace handling; they call fill with either name.trim() ? projectName(name) : '  ' + projectName(name) + '  '. They then call createProject(page, name.trim()). In our code, we trim input.value.trim() before sending, so whitespace should be trimmed. Good.\n\nMaybe the server's POST body parsing: getJsonBody reads data as string and JSON.parse; but request with Content-Type application/json works.\n\nPotential bug: The server's GET /api/projects returns rows ordered by id (SELECT id, name FROM projects ORDER BY id). That's fine.\n\nWhy rows not found? Perhaps the static files not being served for SPA after POST? Not.\n\nLet's try to manually test via curl.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},"output_index":0,"sequence_number":517,"type":"response.output_item.done"}

